# Boiling under DLSS-RR (user report 2026-11-24: the lit scene "lives", lights seem to change every frame). Which input
# DLSS-RR keeps as slow blotches: DI or GI, correlated (lag1 high, RTXDI NoiseAndBias.md) or merely noisy. Target mode
base    di=shipped gi=shipped frame=shipped
seeds   5
cases   cafe.tables sponza.gallery sponza.courtyard
views   Lit "Direct lighting" "Indirect radiance"
kinds   stability
# DI: no reuse (independent per frame), permutation, shorter history, more candidates
sets    di=reference
sets    di.permutation=on
sets    di.history=4
sets    di.history=8
sets    di.localSamples=32
# GI: always decorrelate stagnant samples, shorter history
sets    gi.decorrelationFactor=1
sets    gi.history=4
sets    gi.history=8
# both decorrelated
sets    di=reference gi.decorrelationFactor=1
# the denoiser's model, and the one-bounce mode for comparison
sets    frame.dlssPreset=d
sets    frame.dlssPreset=e
sets    frame.indirectMode=restirGi
